# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# fukuii-project — baseline .gitignore  (hardened superset)
#
# Inherited by every fukuii-project repo via `fukuii-template`. It is a SUPERSET:
# it protects the secret/artifact shapes of every stack we use (JVM/Scala, Node/JS,
# Go, Python, Rust, Docker/infra) because ONE template seeds them all.
#
# RULE: repos are PUBLIC by default. Never remove the SECURITY blocks below.
# Add repo-specific ignores under the marked section at the bottom.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# == SECURITY: secrets & credentials (never commit) ==
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
credentials.json
service-account.json
*.credentials
secrets/
.secrets/
*.secret

# SSH / signing key material — extensionless, so *.pem and *.key do NOT match these.
id_rsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519

# == SECURITY: package-registry auth ==
# A project .npmrc is the standard home for `//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=`,
# and these repos are public. No leading slash, so a nested workspace .npmrc is
# covered too. A policy-only .npmrc is a deliberate decision to take at the time.
.npmrc
.yarnrc
.yarnrc.yml

# == SECURITY: blockchain / node key material ==
/keystore/
wallet.json
mnemonic.txt
*.nodekey
node.key
etc-node.key
jwt.hex
jwtsecret

# == SECURITY: infra / cloud ==
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
*.kubeconfig
kubeconfig
.pgpass
docker-compose.override.yml

# == OS ==
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# == Editors / IDE ==
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.metals/
.bloop/
.bsp/
metals.sbt
.ensime
.ensime_cache/

# == Logs / temp ==
*.log
*.log.*
logs/
tmp/
*.tmp
tmp-*.json
*.pid

# == JVM / Scala / sbt ==
target/
out/
project/boot/
project/plugins/project/
project/project/
project/metals.sbt
*.class

# == Node / JS / TS ==
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.next/
.nuxt/
.turbo/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches

# == Go ==
bin/
*.exe
*.test

# == Python ==
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# == Docs build ==
site/
_site/

# == Nix / direnv ==
result
.direnv/
.nix/

# == Claude Code — agentic tooling ==
# This directory is TRACKED so repo-local agents, skills and rules travel with the
# repo. Only machine-local and agent-written state is held back. Do not invert this
# into a blanket ignore: an agent inside an ignored directory never reaches a clone.
# Committed by design: .claude/settings.json, .claude/{agents,skills,hooks,commands}/,
# AGENTS.md.
#
# Most Claude Code runtime state does live in ~/.claude/, but NOT all of it:
# background agent sessions create git worktrees under .claude/worktrees/, and an
# unignored one lets `git add -A` commit a dangling mode-160000 gitlink into every
# clone. launch.json and scheduled_tasks.json are likewise written in-repo.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/agent-memory-local/
.claude/launch.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/**/*.local.*
.claude/**/*-local/

# == Internal development directory ==
# Session notes, design briefs, dev logs, scratch scripts. Never commit.
.local/

# == Ad-hoc planning docs at root (prefer .local/ going forward) ==
SESSION_NOTES.md
PLANNING.md
SCRATCH.md
*.scratch.*
*.draft.*

# Personal, one-off scratch files with no fleet-wide name still belong in
# `.git/info/exclude` (per-checkout, non-shared) — not a new pattern here.
# .local/ and SESSION_NOTES.md above are the shared convention for that content
# precisely because they are project-wide, not machine-specific.
# Vendored reference repos → git submodules or an out-of-tree bootstrap clone.
# A manually created `git worktree` → a sibling dir OUTSIDE the repo. Claude
# Code's own worktrees are different: created in-repo, ignored above instead.
# Task tracking → GitHub Issues/Projects.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Repo-specific ignores BELOW this line (safe to edit per repo):
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
